      "value": "@{62b61f8ec938a62475e4cd14|full_name}\n\nThank you for your investigation.\n\nAs this is a project currently under construction, we are unable to release all of the code.\n\nAlso, since the prefab data is for sale, we cannot give it to you at this time.\n\nHowever, I think the reason why it is disappearing immediately after being generated is the code part below.\n\nSince the first argument of _Init is not valid, it seems to be discarded on the spot.\n\n```\n\n[UdonBehaviourSyncMode(BehaviourSyncMode.None)]\n\npublic class CostumeMuseumCostume : UdonSharpBehaviour\n\n{\n\n\tbool _isInit;\n\n\tVRCPlayerApi _usePlayer;\n\n\t\n\n\tpublic int UsePlayerId\n\n        {\n\n            get\n\n            {\n\n                if (_usePlayer == null || !_usePlayer.IsValid())\n\n                    return -1;\n\n            \n\n                return _usePlayer.playerId;\n\n            }\n\n        }\n\n\tpublic void _Init(VRCPlayerApi usePlayer, CostumeType costumeType)\n\n        {\n\n            _usePlayer = usePlayer;\n\n            if (!IsValid(_usePlayer))\n\n            {\n\n                DestroyImmediate(gameObject);\n\n                return;\n\n            }\n\n            Networking.SetOwner(usePlayer, gameObject);\n\n            \n\n            foreach (var child in transform.GetComponentsInChildren<Transform>())\n\n            {\n\n                var obj = child.gameObject;\n\n                if (_usePlayer.isLocal && costumeType == CostumeType.Hair)\n\n                {\n\n                    obj.layer = LayerMask.NameToLayer(\"MirrorReflection\");\n\n                }\n\n            }\n\n            _isInit = true;\n\n        }\n\n\tpublic override void PostLateUpdate()\n\n        {\n\n            if (!_isInit)\n\n                return;\n\n            if (!IsValid(_usePlayer))\n\n            {\n\n                DestroyImmediate(gameObject);\n\n            }\n\n            \n\n            TrackingBody();\n\n        }\n\n...\n\n```\n\n`ClothingManager` _Init Method excerpt\n\nIf it has disappeared, I think the call to _ChangeColor will fail.\n\n```\n\nfor (int i = 0; i < MAX_PLAYER_COUNT; i++)\n\n            {\n\n                if (us_playerIds[i] == -1)\n\n                    continue;\n\n                var obj = Instantiate(_costumePrefabs[us_costumeIds[i]], new Vector3(0, 500, 0), Quaternion.identity);\n\n                if (obj)\n\n                {\n\n                    _instanceCostumes[i] = obj.GetComponent<CostumeMuseumCostume>();\n\n                    _instanceCostumes[i]._Init(VRCPlayerApi.GetPlayerById(us_playerIds[i]), _costumeType);\n\nif (i < us_colorValues.Length)\n\n_instanceCostumes[i]._ChangeColor(us_colorValues[i]);\n\n                }\n\n            }\n\n```",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
