      "value": "@{640b9a16bd0441451927c1ba|full_name}: Thanks for the script. Digging in further, it seems on the line `_instanceCostumes[i]._Init(VRCPlayerApi.GetPlayerById(us_playerIds[i]), _costumeType);` you are passing in `0` as the player ID (so `us_playerIds[i]` is `0`) which may not be a valid ID.\n\nI don't see our internal IDs becoming invalid, so this once again looks like an issue in your script somewhere?\n\nBy the way, entirely unrelated, but testing in your world it looks like your prefab also has a bug where it will not work correctly on avatars that don't have Toe bones set ;)",
